{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T07:19:25.665819Z","id":"02be7be0e321cd08c26509738e769e37df34d38c16802ee5a4c08d8b709231ea","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/tests/conformance.rs serves a fake written from https://www.daytona.io/docs/openapi.json and toolbox-openapi.json, so it shares any misreading of them. Not exercised: real start latency, the toolboxProxyUrl of a live sandbox, whether result merges stderr, autoStopInterval units. Run runtime::conformance::check against a live key before relying on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":64},"content_hash":"a55a4c8507871ef7069ad74e43114ca3eaa92c0d46bbc92b4b79016faed354f8"},"summary":"The Daytona client has only run against a fake of its routes, never Daytona itself","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T07:19:25.665883Z","id":"22ba91044990c6a0337f7cd8874204db94b14e3700bd2deb500ccd3558ba0564","body":{"detail":"A resumed run calls exec on an empty map and gets a new container with a fresh checkout, so edits made before the restart are gone with no error, and the old container runs until the runtime's auto-stop. The clax.run label is set at create, so finding it again through ContainerRuntime::attach is the likely fix.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":67},"content_hash":"d3b1e567969d215f7381574c1d26f2289c0a6e4c140fcc010dd6581369e2ad77"},"summary":"Run-to-container state is in memory: a daemon restart loses it mid-run","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T07:19:25.665907Z","id":"6044047b981e63e9c74a1e1ef9d8d3859ed827a8f7af52422909c6c6c9db6044","body":{"detail":"change.propose does not answer until the preview serves the commit. The demo's preview is up in a second. A real Clax preview takes many minutes (.github/workflows/preview.yml has timeout-minutes: 60), and how a host call that long sits with the run's lease and step limits in crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs is untested. Returning at once and proposing the fix when the preview is up may be the better shape.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":289},"end":{"line":289},"content_hash":"e1b5cca3cfe1f83db006ca9facc1a8c255979b59bd9cd7ee201fdc4bfb22ce6e"},"summary":"The preview wait blocks inside one script call for up to preview_timeout_secs","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T07:19:25.665938Z","id":"786fdb466b0e3cf12aa902c2f1c77d9718b32696991d74ce6927bcbc2ac4ab0d","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md says never push unsigned commits, and a repository that requires signatures will refuse these. A deployment needs an identity that can sign, such as commits made through the forge's API by a GitHub App, which it signs itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"a84ad638b1986be48f6198d08e7b49c4d4ff741ac63c4f6e9af1a5aeaabd6a0a"},"summary":"ClaxBot's commits are unsigned","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T07:19:25.666064Z","id":"6b7ac2ebe5c57f7d1aef142590ec86f2eb91dac580734546894166e40ae6857e","body":{"detail":"GitHub does not start workflows for events made with GITHUB_TOKEN, so write_token_env must hold a GitHub App or personal token for .github/workflows/preview.yml to run. The demo's forge deploys by itself and does not show this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":96},"end":{"line":113}},"summary":"A pull request opened with the Actions GITHUB_TOKEN would start no preview","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T07:19:25.666289Z","id":"4cb8c42c3bc8015e3e190b895fd2fdae9f21ef4defe038fc605e880b15211210","body":{"detail":"ContainerSpec::domain_allow_list reaches Daytona only. A container holds no credential, but a run steered by a report could send the checkout anywhere. Docker needs a network policy of its own before it runs anything but a public repository.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"8cb32bc382aa04036d77bed68236f9e29fea3bcc71b75dbf29e521bce5145786"},"summary":"The Docker runtime ignores domain_allow_list, so its containers have open egress","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T13:43:38.120143Z","id":"bba6511c9693e391eb8b4060dfb7037c0f2e58786555fa6af1045fbe74b1bb21","body":{"detail":"docker exec --env K=V carries the value on the command line, which crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs:7 says a token must not do. The value is the base64 of x-access-token:<token> from repo::token_env. Pass --env K with no value and set it on the docker process's own environment.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":94},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"9c1814ca273069ea60df4a232104003e82a8c87281f5fccbc6192e0644fee03e"},"summary":"The Docker runtime puts exec envs in argv, so a read token shows in the host's process list","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T13:43:38.148306Z","id":"58377ec964e09661eef48cef092f2a8d2ca6909b37209e93a74acbf6c66c53f9","body":{"detail":"No test or demo sets read_token_env: demo/claxbot-workspace/run.ts clones a local path with no authentication, so repo::token_env has never met an authenticated remote. Separately, a run on a private target reads the source while following reporter text, and what it writes on the report's thread reaches that reporter, so private code can leave without any network egress. Neither domain_allow_list nor protected_paths covers that channel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":150},"end":{"line":154},"content_hash":"f180c3c9b9083b157f97aaac7c26d8abf0c6ebb112a0aa63fb44c73f18a4564f"},"summary":"The private-repository path has no test, and a reporter can steer a model that reads private source","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.203498Z","id":"770cb2866a1737eaced1bd920833522024f3a7da0f0b6c0cc6f2285d7b23676d","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"docker exec now passes --env K and sets the value on the docker process. Evidence: docker::tests::an_env_value_never_reaches_argv passes, and docker_keeps_the_contract passes against a real daemon, so the value still reaches the command.","supersedes":"bba6511c9693e391eb8b4060dfb7037c0f2e58786555fa6af1045fbe74b1bb21","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.373711Z","id":"61b946fa811271db500eeeb3b2d39c7708bc263ac6b39f6d414404ba162fdc40","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"An allow-list is no longer ignored: ContainerRuntime::limits_domains is part of the contract, Docker::create refuses a non-empty list, and runtime::conformance::check fails a runtime that runs open under one. Evidence: docker::tests::a_spec_with_an_allow_list_is_refused_before_anything_runs and docker_keeps_the_contract pass. What an empty list means on Docker is its own record.","supersedes":"4cb8c42c3bc8015e3e190b895fd2fdae9f21ef4defe038fc605e880b15211210","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.536901Z","id":"cfedc25ae05664bec19ebec8278277ad68f6e34d174739ba990dbb3bcf03af46","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"A run with nothing in memory now finds its container by the clax.run label, reattaches, and rebuilds the host clone from the clax.base and clax.queue labels; failing that it is told the workspace was lost. Evidence: recovery::a_restarted_daemon_finds_a_runs_container_and_its_edits, recovery::a_container_gone_altogether_is_lost_and_never_silently_remade, and recovery::a_real_container_survives_a_restart_and_its_change_is_pushed (real Docker) pass. Wiring the ledger and reap into the daemon is its own record.","supersedes":"22ba91044990c6a0337f7cd8874204db94b14e3700bd2deb500ccd3558ba0564","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.709799Z","id":"7373a92967b78b94eaa53f05f0d3c6c9f5494c8df253cb52b5fdf7aee36b9099","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"58377ec964e09661eef48cef092f2a8d2ca6909b37209e93a74acbf6c66c53f9","summary":"The first half is covered: crates/clax-bot-workspace/tests/conformance/auth.rs and recovery.rs run a real git against git http-backend behind a server that answers 401 without the token, for the host's clone and the container's. The reporter-steering half of this record is untouched by that.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.710311Z","id":"d0ddf8aaa2082565179478a600e42202e07c8b45b9b4b99227a145c47915be3b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"02be7be0e321cd08c26509738e769e37df34d38c16802ee5a4c08d8b709231ea","summary":"Still never run against Daytona. live_daytona_keeps_the_contract in crates/clax-bot-workspace/tests/conformance/daytona.rs proves it when a key exists: DAYTONA_API_KEY=... bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot-workspace:conformance --test_env=DAYTONA_API_KEY --test_arg=live_daytona --test_output=all. Assumptions added here that only that run can test: an absent exitCode means 0; POST /sandbox/{id}/start may repeat on a 5xx; label keys with dots are accepted; GET /sandbox labels filter matches on all pairs (find also rechecks them itself); 429 and Retry-After, which openapi.json does not document on these routes, are how its rate limits show.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.710391Z","id":"83cd50d9994db5e79634fa3f91f7e4a84150c67cc3230682d7c129a5bc39cbc6","body":{"detail":"Failure: a daemon restarts, a run's container is gone (deleted, or never listed), and config::for_home built the workspace without with_ledger: recover finds nothing, cannot tell the run from a new one, and it gets a fresh checkout with its edits silently gone. Every other loss is reported without the ledger. The fix is one call in crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs for_home: .with_ledger(home.join(\"workspace-runs\")).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":158},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"7d5d24c1752717a8a542221bd76f1004784515c69073751d817bba48077fe5f8"},"summary":"The run ledger is off until the daemon turns it on","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.710436Z","id":"5bc9fdeb087780147db4d27d53cfe8ed3f512528ec0303297796451f01185310","body":{"detail":"ContainerWorkspace::reap needs a caller in the daemon, passing every run that may still resume; clax_bot::Workspace has no such hook. Until then a container whose run ended during a restart lives until its runtime stops it. Before it is wired, crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs must put a value unique to the home in the clax.workspace label: it is \"1\" for everyone, so two daemons sharing a Daytona organization or a Docker host would each end the other's live containers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":387},"end":{"line":401},"content_hash":"0111844cf032e4ce61cb627c87ce1abc4da9bbdf0056e9d0a91b226d4ca62ba6"},"summary":"Nothing calls reap yet, and the label that scopes it does not tell two deployments apart","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.710475Z","id":"80048d3b67c8bb77efc3732ed82c06e9f2e4be814fa7eeabccfdfa903d8b3ce4","body":{"detail":"A non-empty domain_allow_list is refused, but the empty list, which demo/claxbot-workspace/run.ts relies on, leaves a container on Docker's default network. A run steered by a report can send the checkout anywhere. run_args can give it --network none or a filtering network, and a clone from a mount still works under those; nothing requires it. Should a target with a read token on a runtime that cannot limit egress be refused at startup?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"214494ebe9a14eb475238a72f63e1fe84bc1812f1b4261d698256fd15ec20572"},"summary":"An empty allow-list on Docker is open egress","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.710506Z","id":"6526acdb01497c6c5186b68f8230a1086ed92be386dcbf73ef937f8a0158b022","body":{"detail":"sleep N ends a container N minutes after it started however busy it is, and a run holding it in memory then gets shell_unavailable from every exec until a restart reattaches it (attach starts it again). Daytona's autoStopInterval has the same effect on a held sandbox after an idle stretch. Reattaching on that error would serve both, but exec is not safe to repeat blindly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":130},"end":{"line":133},"content_hash":"56b46aae20d275af7fb61f18ece70c4f208f9116401c1278ee66c19e6e2fdfa3"},"summary":"Docker's auto-stop is a lifetime, not an idle limit","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.710547Z","id":"b11b9d0541dac88a32ac172e804d972feee8e90f16f95c3927752cf9c7100318","body":{"detail":"binary_refusal refuses every delta hunk, because a small delta can expand without limit and only inflating it shows how far, so a change to an existing binary file cannot be proposed, while a new one can. git diff --binary has no way to force literal hunks. Inflating deltas here needs a dependency, and rlimits on the child differ by platform.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":110},"content_hash":"66b42e258645ca83ba26d0f53c3ab570541161afe5e259f8f959a25903b517e5"},"summary":"Allowing binary deltas under a resource limit on git apply","tags":["revisit:a target whose fixes need to change binary files","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:20:59.710576Z","id":"ad330f5c7b72499fd1942fd8db2836319e6d1a907c8ccc3671bf7a15e9035451","body":{"detail":"It holds for what git and a remote quote: the token and its Basic credentials. An image that re-encodes the read token during the clone command can still print it, since that command runs in the container with the token in its environment. Tokens are short-lived and scoped to one repository for this reason; the image is the operator's choice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":83},"content_hash":"8384b7cd510aacdd0c1ae8971f5bf94155bbbb56f419869c5dad780269fae34f"},"summary":"redact matches a token's literal forms only","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:25:24.709569Z","id":"7a9e7c52f1526959475537a4f1d961ea0bac51b7e646e9c9a488dc7efc6fd79d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6044047b981e63e9c74a1e1ef9d8d3859ed827a8f7af52422909c6c6c9db6044","summary":"Measured, not fixed here. A call of many minutes is safe for the run: watched() renews the claim beside the script, host time counts against no script limit, and it is one step (crates/clax-bot/tests/workspace.rs, a_propose_of_many_minutes_keeps_the_runs_claim_and_takes_one_step). It still holds a driver slot, and a run past max_run_minutes stops at the cap after the call, without a finish turn (a_propose_that_outlasts_the_runs_time_keeps_its_fix_and_the_run_stops_at_the_cap). The seam to end the wait exists: Workspace::previews gives a PreviewSink, which reaches BotHost::preview_ready.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T14:25:24.709980Z","id":"624b339681e524680e3f30a8cc4606efb1c3947bd0257bb1ec3f705c2bb040fe","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"58377ec964e09661eef48cef092f2a8d2ca6909b37209e93a74acbf6c66c53f9","summary":"The steering is now bounded on ClaxBot's side: Offer::confidential makes every reply and notice members-only, reduces a fix to fixed words and verify_url, and refuses publish, db writes and web calls (crates/clax-bot/tests/workspace.rs, a_confidential_run_can_write_nothing_a_reporter_reads_but_fixed_words_and_a_link). ContainerWorkspace::offer does not set it yet: a target with a read token should answer Offer::CHANGE.confidential().","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:12.637721Z","id":"812f1dbea888a84dcbb61e7d120d675286a0fb561f8a3a3746445eb8b1383858","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"config::for_home now reaches Config::open, which calls with_ledger(home.join(\"workspace-runs\")), and a workspace without one keeps a temporary ledger for its own life. Evidence: recovery::a_container_gone_altogether_is_lost_and_never_silently_remade passes.","supersedes":"83cd50d9994db5e79634fa3f91f7e4a84150c67cc3230682d7c129a5bc39cbc6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:12.787824Z","id":"bd3632712fccf57d345fb1ad7e37c81f865700528a1f3d2316ad7db2dcf7828c","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"clax_bot::Workspace::reap is implemented over ContainerWorkspace::end_finished and clax.workspace now holds a value kept per home in <home>/workspace-id. Evidence: recovery::reap_ends_only_what_is_this_deployments_and_over and config::tests::a_home_keeps_its_own_deployment_id pass.","supersedes":"5bc9fdeb087780147db4d27d53cfe8ed3f512528ec0303297796451f01185310","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:12.938294Z","id":"3bb53dbd3501355c80fbeaa9e5df65fe303cb89306e0b923d34674b810153122","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"A container now ends by docker::idle_watch, marked active by every command, and an exec that answers Err clears the held container so the next call takes it back through attach. Evidence: an_idle_watch_ends_on_its_own (real Docker) and recovery::a_container_that_stops_under_a_run_comes_back_at_the_next_call pass.","supersedes":"6526acdb01497c6c5186b68f8230a1086ed92be386dcbf73ef937f8a0158b022","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:13.081394Z","id":"9d5319889462ee78ee8ce8bcec4e79147d33118f94d72d98d4d4397344f1735f","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"propose answers at once with verify_url null and a detached task tells the PreviewSink, holding no lock of the run's. Evidence: recovery::a_preview_that_never_answers_does_not_hold_up_a_proposal, recovery::a_preview_is_told_of_after_the_proposal_and_after_the_run and recovery::a_second_proposal_supersedes_the_wait_for_the_first pass.","supersedes":"6044047b981e63e9c74a1e1ef9d8d3859ed827a8f7af52422909c6c6c9db6044","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/docker.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:13.222437Z","id":"15e8afdc27d60aa91196890d5ff0e65b85220051c8e03a9579e34a33b39ca2c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Config::check_egress fails at startup for a confidential target with no allow-list a runtime enforces, unless allow_open_egress says otherwise, and a target is confidential unless public. A public target on Docker keeps open egress by configuration. Evidence: config::tests::a_confidential_target_needs_egress_held_or_said_to_be_open passes.","supersedes":"80048d3b67c8bb77efc3732ed82c06e9f2e4be814fa7eeabccfdfa903d8b3ce4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:13.364630Z","id":"ffd9f35276874a1dfa4baecc1764e7a8d3ba98e6ed7dcd6794d1d58a7b062368","body":{"detail":"It holds for what git and a remote quote: the token and its Basic credentials. An image that re-encodes the read token during the clone command can still print it, since that command runs in the container with the token in its environment. How much that matters depends on crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs RepoAccess: StaticAccess, the only implementation so far, gives a long-lived token from the environment, so a target should use a read-only one scoped to its repository until a short-lived source exists. The image is the operator's choice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":223},"content_hash":"5c3ca6b97857ec9f0caf5dea61b2d3647e0eedb6b231c51ed2f17626496fe47f"},"summary":"redact matches a token's literal forms only","supersedes":"ad330f5c7b72499fd1942fd8db2836319e6d1a907c8ccc3671bf7a15e9035451","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:13.506016Z","id":"184be38459957d3c5b73c389fd731be830a11c9ca17c93eee02b25158aef5e7d","body":{"detail":"binary_refusal refuses every delta hunk, because a small delta can expand without limit and only inflating it shows how far, so a change to an existing binary file cannot be proposed, while a new one can. git diff --binary has no way to force literal hunks. Inflating deltas here needs a dependency, and rlimits on the child differ by platform.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":227},"end":{"line":259},"content_hash":"419d7f10d46a551f35be891133147a33eee0191b245f71483fe3925dd29c457c"},"summary":"Allowing binary deltas under a resource limit on git apply","supersedes":"b11b9d0541dac88a32ac172e804d972feee8e90f16f95c3927752cf9c7100318","tags":["revisit:a target whose fixes need to change binary files","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:13.662710Z","id":"c6de93629af80760170548ec2b0666371f1770b2a26ba74ce5aa045156ae3c1f","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md says never push unsigned commits, and a repository that requires signatures will refuse these. A deployment needs an identity that can sign, such as commits made through the forge's API by a GitHub App, which it signs itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":580},"end":{"line":607},"content_hash":"76245c432f143dcf31e9748fb2d7b7b42c2d70241382e83e7e9f646f453172f7"},"summary":"ClaxBot's commits are unsigned","supersedes":"786fdb466b0e3cf12aa902c2f1c77d9718b32696991d74ce6927bcbc2ac4ab0d","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:13.805800Z","id":"a0c67f17e925e63584bf7351fe1765e0fb5ff28d6cc77fa36f1efcdd1860eee3","body":{"detail":"No test or demo sets read_token_env: demo/claxbot-workspace/run.ts clones a local path with no authentication, so repo::token_env has never met an authenticated remote. Separately, a run on a private target reads the source while following reporter text, and what it writes on the report's thread reaches that reporter, so private code can leave without any network egress. Neither domain_allow_list nor protected_paths covers that channel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":324},"end":{"line":338},"content_hash":"b08da3ab1da62e92c9bad75712e7c2163413494a36a6976374b215c01fbc0929"},"summary":"The private-repository path has no test, and a reporter can steer a model that reads private source","supersedes":"58377ec964e09661eef48cef092f2a8d2ca6909b37209e93a74acbf6c66c53f9","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:13.947890Z","id":"dc25d9bf379ae52c66ca89703b0db5e3f571e046e58c0adaf9d6890ad32b7933","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/tests/conformance.rs serves a fake written from https://www.daytona.io/docs/openapi.json and toolbox-openapi.json, so it shares any misreading of them. Not exercised: real start latency, the toolboxProxyUrl of a live sandbox, whether result merges stderr, autoStopInterval units. Run runtime::conformance::check against a live key before relying on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":97},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"50f3ff2f80763ecc84a31cc0622d3e23f811325052a3fa36f40944bd453397b1"},"summary":"The Daytona client has only run against a fake of its routes, never Daytona itself","supersedes":"02be7be0e321cd08c26509738e769e37df34d38c16802ee5a4c08d8b709231ea","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:14.089626Z","id":"d0f7559c2621694afbb961bd8a08f5355131da6f2a92a7dbec52daa428b275b5","body":{"detail":"GitHub does not start workflows for events made with GITHUB_TOKEN, so write_token_env must hold a GitHub App or personal token for .github/workflows/preview.yml to run. The demo's forge deploys by itself and does not show this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"11a280f1711ed4b91fbc7243f425df8cd57d897b6c41884fa7941420492cd4b3"},"summary":"A pull request opened with the Actions GITHUB_TOKEN would start no preview","supersedes":"6b7ac2ebe5c57f7d1aef142590ec86f2eb91dac580734546894166e40ae6857e","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:14.231096Z","id":"302a13d56f329014d58861ba6393b12e7ceffe99009c205104a42a2e5f87d91b","body":{"detail":"The detached task in ContainerWorkspace::watch_preview lives in the daemon's process. A daemon that restarts during a wait tells nobody when the preview comes up, and a reporter gets no link until a person looks. The ledger could hold the pull request and commit, and Workspace::previews could start the waits again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":447},"end":{"line":450},"content_hash":"b65e41905197e12099bb15d09797fa37b4319945704a583fc9244cb47231c4ce"},"summary":"A wait for a preview does not survive a restart","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:02:14.231143Z","id":"b0a1ee439cc7fd8d6c8e1ed05f16a16faa64d7aef9f5df53f7c227038d5f03f3","body":{"detail":"holds_egress compares domainAllowList and networkPolicyError when a sandbox starts and when it is attached. networkPolicyError is the outcome of the most recent policy change, so one that fails later during a run goes unseen until the next attach. Whether Daytona echoes the list as sent, rather than normalized, has not been seen against the live service: a difference would refuse every sandbox, which is the safe way to be wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":277},"content_hash":"5f9e7a31043d47d84a590173bfd32e8114d2f8eaa643521afc5dd6389c6b8e7b"},"summary":"The egress check reads Daytona's report at start and attach, not after","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:56.347561Z","id":"f01e0431f6af550d48d1d89e335f0292b649c7757d8f8b659a96eec4a1a11cd5","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The ledger keeps each run's latest wait with its deadline, and Workspace::previews takes them up for what is left. Evidence: recovery::a_restart_takes_up_the_wait_for_a_preview passes.","supersedes":"302a13d56f329014d58861ba6393b12e7ceffe99009c205104a42a2e5f87d91b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:56.599901Z","id":"8ab1456eff59cf9efede309ea4ae22b03d0f6082f608a287635a6a4d483ea2bc","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/tests/conformance.rs serves a fake written from https://www.daytona.io/docs/openapi.json and toolbox-openapi.json, so it shares any misreading of them. Not exercised: real start latency, the toolboxProxyUrl of a live sandbox, whether result merges stderr, autoStopInterval units. Run runtime::conformance::check against a live key before relying on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":97},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"50f3ff2f80763ecc84a31cc0622d3e23f811325052a3fa36f40944bd453397b1"},"summary":"The Daytona client has only run against a fake of its routes, never Daytona itself","supersedes":"dc25d9bf379ae52c66ca89703b0db5e3f571e046e58c0adaf9d6890ad32b7933","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:56.836317Z","id":"25af8d0c635e5d794df055d7e830f01899f414937aeeb5f547aa1cd448fccedd","body":{"detail":"holds_egress compares domainAllowList and networkPolicyError when a sandbox starts and when it is attached. networkPolicyError is the outcome of the most recent policy change, so one that fails later during a run goes unseen until the next attach. Whether Daytona echoes the list as sent, rather than normalized, has not been seen against the live service: a difference would refuse every sandbox, which is the safe way to be wrong.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":265},"end":{"line":267},"content_hash":"5f9e7a31043d47d84a590173bfd32e8114d2f8eaa643521afc5dd6389c6b8e7b"},"summary":"The egress check reads Daytona's report at start and attach, not after","supersedes":"b0a1ee439cc7fd8d6c8e1ed05f16a16faa64d7aef9f5df53f7c227038d5f03f3","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:57.071145Z","id":"bf8b6db0fd8d6c04f07223a74dc5be55df20fb0e9b1ee3c774b71faa787f8bb2","body":{"detail":"GitHub does not start workflows for events made with GITHUB_TOKEN, so write_token_env must hold a GitHub App or personal token for .github/workflows/preview.yml to run. The demo's forge deploys by itself and does not show this.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":131},"content_hash":"11a280f1711ed4b91fbc7243f425df8cd57d897b6c41884fa7941420492cd4b3"},"summary":"A pull request opened with the Actions GITHUB_TOKEN would start no preview","supersedes":"d0f7559c2621694afbb961bd8a08f5355131da6f2a92a7dbec52daa428b275b5","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:57.291006Z","id":"8aa8a52043921e1ba51da4bec1e439c6450946dd73cbc6b0009957702925f32a","body":{"detail":"It holds for what git and a remote quote: the token and its Basic credentials. An image that re-encodes the read token during the clone command can still print it, since that command runs in the container with the token in its environment. How much that matters depends on crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs RepoAccess: StaticAccess, the only implementation so far, gives a long-lived token from the environment, so a target should use a read-only one scoped to its repository until a short-lived source exists. The image is the operator's choice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":217},"end":{"line":229},"content_hash":"5c3ca6b97857ec9f0caf5dea61b2d3647e0eedb6b231c51ed2f17626496fe47f"},"summary":"redact matches a token's literal forms only","supersedes":"ffd9f35276874a1dfa4baecc1764e7a8d3ba98e6ed7dcd6794d1d58a7b062368","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:57.498584Z","id":"49106f5c33f5c5e337865f0ce41a781702dc23b3c5941af07cc672987d842de1","body":{"detail":"binary_refusal refuses every delta hunk, because a small delta can expand without limit and only inflating it shows how far, so a change to an existing binary file cannot be proposed, while a new one can. git diff --binary has no way to force literal hunks. Inflating deltas here needs a dependency, and rlimits on the child differ by platform.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":233},"end":{"line":265},"content_hash":"419d7f10d46a551f35be891133147a33eee0191b245f71483fe3925dd29c457c"},"summary":"Allowing binary deltas under a resource limit on git apply","supersedes":"184be38459957d3c5b73c389fd731be830a11c9ca17c93eee02b25158aef5e7d","tags":["revisit:a target whose fixes need to change binary files","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:57.720384Z","id":"cebb213dad28231971b6793874ddc752bf12070e6369d3ebd4f1eb36e3df25ca","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md says never push unsigned commits, and a repository that requires signatures will refuse these. A deployment needs an identity that can sign, such as commits made through the forge's API by a GitHub App, which it signs itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":582},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"882409562b0524b2a5c60901bf3356fbb4f9ba75a5ff6422285a11605d23b67c"},"summary":"ClaxBot's commits are unsigned","supersedes":"c6de93629af80760170548ec2b0666371f1770b2a26ba74ce5aa045156ae3c1f","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:57.934254Z","id":"b416f9a39bb5a9a28720865f9f74e633d76e1dd620fdc1b168cb2d1c19ca4cf1","body":{"detail":"No test or demo sets read_token_env: demo/claxbot-workspace/run.ts clones a local path with no authentication, so repo::token_env has never met an authenticated remote. Separately, a run on a private target reads the source while following reporter text, and what it writes on the report's thread reaches that reporter, so private code can leave without any network egress. Neither domain_allow_list nor protected_paths covers that channel.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":344},"end":{"line":358},"content_hash":"d8901e7ffd4b9e357320033c47185ade269e1b2dddde2c8607f335d626097962"},"summary":"The private-repository path has no test, and a reporter can steer a model that reads private source","supersedes":"a0c67f17e925e63584bf7351fe1765e0fb5ff28d6cc77fa36f1efcdd1860eee3","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:28:58.135799Z","id":"965a0caefcbafcbdd96a7b8d5ebd48466fa1ad53b33a6be729c43c279f330493","body":{"detail":"check_egress counts any non-empty list on an enforcing runtime as enough for a confidential target. A list with a host that takes uploads does not keep source private: with github.com, as in deploy/claxbot-workspace/clax.toml, a steered model can git push the checkout to a repository of an attacker's, and registries and paste hosts are the same. The config docs and the error text say so. Holding it would take a proxy that limits by path and method, a package mirror in place of the general hosts, or no egress for confidential runs. Which should a confidential target require?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":225},"end":{"line":246},"content_hash":"ac6bfcd555accf7cbc49c36b04bbd04efc4159ec635102ade6549d7ac951ff26"},"summary":"An allow-list of general hosts does not hold confidentiality","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:49:06.920757Z","id":"10bce41f61b04541c7d91800406828e5d31c1fafa3ba2c07aec985305b1f2ec9","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"A target with [target.github_app] no longer commits with git: Forge::commit and Forge::advance make the commit through GitHub's Git Data API with no author, committer or signature, which is what GitHub documents for a bot signature. A target with a token must say allow_unsigned_commits = true or fails at parse. Evidence: github::a_change_is_committed_by_the_forge_with_nothing_of_ours_on_the_commit and config::tests::a_token_pushes_unsigned_commits_only_when_told_it_may pass. That shows the request's shape against a fake, not GitHub's signature; what only a live run can confirm is its own record on crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs.","supersedes":"cebb213dad28231971b6793874ddc752bf12070e6369d3ebd4f1eb36e3df25ca","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:49:07.060756Z","id":"97f53f2c7c2ba61cccfd00ca08d5b8afcf943143a15fa4bc2e667cd84f3cc859","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8aa8a52043921e1ba51da4bec1e439c6450946dd73cbc6b0009957702925f32a","summary":"StaticAccess is no longer the only source: crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/github_app.rs mints read tokens of one hour, contents: read, on one repository. The literal-forms limit of redact stands, and a read token from write_token_env's sibling read_token_env is still long-lived.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:49:07.061136Z","id":"dd595d77fb16ba7657e1be11e280ad110ec7b04b0a62454f9ee0b9e724fe4e7b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"bf8b6db0fd8d6c04f07223a74dc5be55df20fb0e9b1ee3c774b71faa787f8bb2","summary":"Checked against https://docs.github.com/en/actions/concepts/security/github_token: to have workflow runs from a pull request go without approval, it says to use a GitHub App installation access token or a personal access token instead of GITHUB_TOKEN, so a [target.github_app] target's pull request starts preview.yml. This record's wording is out of date in one respect: the page now says pull_request events (opened, synchronize, reopened) from GITHUB_TOKEN create runs in an approval-required state, rather than none, while other events create no run. That page speaks of pull requests; that a ref moved by PATCH /git/refs with an App token fires synchronize has not been seen live.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:49:07.061198Z","id":"13391fd8dce2a72ec17fc144d8d7d8a28fee8bc46f74929176bf55f74105bc59","body":{"detail":"https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/managing-commit-signature-verification/about-commit-signature-verification says a bot's commit is verified when the request is authenticated as the GitHub App and carries no custom author, committer or signature, naming the Commits API. crates/clax-bot-workspace/tests/conformance/github.rs serves a fake, so these are unconfirmed until a live run: that POST /git/commits answers verification.verified true at once rather than later (a false answer only logs a warning here, because refusing on it could refuse every commit if GitHub fills it in afterwards); that an installation token issued with repositories and permissions narrowed still counts; which status a non-fast-forward PATCH and an existing ref's POST answer; that git fetch sees a ref straight after the API moved it; and how a file replaced by a directory of the same name goes through base_tree, where a wrong answer is refused by the tree comparison at line 265 rather than committed. GitHub documents nothing about a personal access token's API commits, so a token is taken as unsigned and pushes with git. Run one proposal on a scratch repository with a real App and read verification on the commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":245},"end":{"line":283},"content_hash":"279ce01b4eabe35d3b3ccfc0df5a2d788d895b9d8d2c11d9f96e830646b310af"},"summary":"That GitHub marks an App's API commit verified is documented, and has not been seen","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/github_app.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:49:07.061233Z","id":"16bb6faa6425c64019521ff0fa2805f0c33ebd019661c1ed000af9735a3cb5e4","body":{"detail":"GitHubAppAccess keeps the read token until TOKEN_MARGIN_SECS before it expires, so runs in that stretch of up to fifty minutes share one token, and a container that kept it could read the repository for that long. It reaches a container only in the environment of the clone command (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs check_out), so this takes a hostile image. Not caching the read token gives each container its own at the price of one call per run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":237},"content_hash":"e07233e2343f648455837038d6c09cac23ba2d889dd24ec56ad54e283fcc5f12"},"summary":"A cached read token is handed to every container of a repository while it lasts","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T15:49:07.061278Z","id":"7152c48d03acfae2d59495868fbf69d9515848686cf472c2f5cd67ad9eb97002","body":{"detail":"TargetConfig::check_credentials refuses a token without allow_unsigned_commits. A Target built any other way, as a queue's repository link will be from clax_store::queue_repos::RepoCredentials::Token, gets git push with no such check. That wiring has to decide: refuse the link, or carry an allowance. RepoCredentials::GithubApp maps to GitHubAppAccess and GitHub::new(..).committing().","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":256},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"d0b7d87610c1348441e8fc6ceb07576985e4d157bb3e7fe0584e38414081a66c"},"summary":"Unsigned pushes are refused in workspace.toml only, not on Target","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:08:51.871077Z","id":"358e1d23d350aaca62e02357df25d4a83f072c71832f25e2fe74166e070e23cb","body":{"detail":"https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/managing-commit-signature-verification/about-commit-signature-verification says a bot's commit is verified when the request is authenticated as the GitHub App and carries no custom author, committer or signature, naming the Commits API. A false or missing verification.verified now refuses the commit unless Target::unsigned is Allow, after GitHub::verified_later reads it VERIFY_ATTEMPTS (3) times, VERIFY_DELAY (2s) apart. GitHub documents no moment at which verification is settled, so those numbers are a guess, and the one live proposal decides whether they are right: if GitHub settles it later than that, every commit of an App target is refused and stays on no branch. crates/clax-bot-workspace/tests/conformance/github.rs serves a fake, so also unconfirmed until that run: that an installation token narrowed by repositories and permissions still counts; which status a non-fast-forward PATCH and an existing ref's POST answer; that git fetch sees a ref straight after the API moved it; that DELETE /installation/token answers 204 for a token narrowed this way; and how a file replaced by a directory of the same name goes through base_tree, where a wrong answer is refused by the tree comparison in GitHub::commit rather than committed. GitHub documents nothing about a personal access token's API commits, so a token is taken as unsigned. Run one proposal on a scratch repository with a real App and read verification on the commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":326},"end":{"line":369},"content_hash":"abb189c63c24890cca853bca43db68d934d366105d0dcd7a0aeb0791c28ab7e4"},"summary":"That GitHub marks an App's API commit verified is documented, and has not been seen, and one live proposal decides whether the re-read bound is right","supersedes":"13391fd8dce2a72ec17fc144d8d7d8a28fee8bc46f74929176bf55f74105bc59","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/github_app.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:08:52.011681Z","id":"b50b65d1a63df1668e44b2dc46b7da12c2432321041954691196c20c216811a7","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Read tokens are no longer kept: each clone mints one, and ContainerWorkspace::check_out ends it through RepoAccess::revoke_read as soon as the clone command returns, also on failure. Evidence: github::each_clone_has_a_read_token_of_its_own_ended_when_it_returns, github::a_clone_that_fails_still_ends_its_token, github::a_revocation_that_fails_does_not_stop_the_run and github::a_read_token_is_never_kept pass.","supersedes":"16bb6faa6425c64019521ff0fa2805f0c33ebd019661c1ed000af9735a3cb5e4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:08:52.153563Z","id":"27e703691812cc7df7cb89ae8d0294c1211ebeed2fbbfca787d04824ec9f0fc6","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"The check is no longer in config: Target::unsigned is a required field with no default, ContainerWorkspace::publish refuses a push and commit_by_forge an unverified commit unless it is Allow, and allow_unsigned_commits only sets it. A queue's Target has to name it, so this record's question is now answered where each Target is built. Evidence: recovery::a_push_nobody_signed_is_refused_unless_the_target_allows_it, github::a_commit_never_verified_stays_on_no_branch and config::tests::allow_unsigned_commits_says_what_a_target_carries_and_nothing_else pass.","supersedes":"7152c48d03acfae2d59495868fbf69d9515848686cf472c2f5cd67ad9eb97002","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:08:52.293174Z","id":"6b7040b7512d107644486dd63ac9a8c852875d521e90b9e32d047331ddc1444f","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"10bce41f61b04541c7d91800406828e5d31c1fafa3ba2c07aec985305b1f2ec9","summary":"Corrected by later work: a token target no longer fails at parse, and config::tests::a_token_pushes_unsigned_commits_only_when_told_it_may is gone. Target::unsigned refuses at propose instead, and an unverified commit from the forge is refused too; recovery::a_push_nobody_signed_is_refused_unless_the_target_allows_it and github::a_commit_never_verified_stays_on_no_branch cover it.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:48:33.941355Z","id":"589475611cfeb256b783fe3141095a8f3c8c31ed806dd2b49d94ec9c86466ffb","body":{"detail":"PublicOnly::pin hands git its checked answers with -c http.curloptResolve, which git added in 2.37; an older git ignores an unknown setting, resolves for itself, and a name that changes between the check and the connection reaches what it answers. git 2.54 was tested (linked::every_git_command_goes_to_the_pinned_address_and_is_checked_anew reaches a .invalid name through the pin alone). The daemon does not check the git version: a hosted deployment's image must carry 2.37 or later.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"1c3ba091a0f64c5231514c9dd7511f7f24951f48013725c4440e8424c3601083"},"summary":"A git older than 2.37 ignores http.curloptResolve, leaving a check-then-use race on a link's host","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:48:33.941408Z","id":"d7bfeff3f44a30e8c601b05e69bcfc633fcf4742682b67a9cf41241b978e558b","body":{"detail":"reqwest honours the system proxy and repo.rs GIT_ENV keeps http_proxy and friends, so with a proxy set neither the client's resolver nor the git pin decides where a connection goes: the proxy does, and a private answer is not refused. Turning proxies off for held links would break a hosted daemon that needs one to leave its network, so this is left to the operator and said in net.rs and in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-06-claxbot-workspace-design.md section 4.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"468fb34392a0df23201bad200c60076ac30a74893d0e7861b0d517caa3cef995"},"summary":"A proxy in the daemon's environment resolves a link's names itself, past PublicOnly","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:48:33.941566Z","id":"395439cb7bd43d6fdc912e0d7356e7e92d53a88e2fab2b209dee7b45e0f84171","body":{"detail":"GitHubAppAccess is opened per run, so each run mints its own write token and drops it at Workspace::finish without calling DELETE /installation/token. It never leaves the daemon. Revoking would need a hook on RepoAccess and care for a preview wait or a resumed run that still holds the target.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":131},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"ee7be3fb4c933a7eaf7fac3629c6c2f3d94834921991ff98b8c7ffd5006ce61e"},"summary":"An App link's write token is not revoked when its run ends; it lapses within the hour in the daemon's memory","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T16:48:33.942022Z","id":"8641bd89891cd371283a8db647bcd96e79db1885a940879d4efde0912ed6d536","body":{"detail":"Config::check_image refuses a [[target]] on Docker with no image, since the default image has no git, but a link is unknown at boot. The run is told the container could not be reached and the panel shows that the container could not clone the repository.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":317},"content_hash":"0c6030392e9e446e6b5ac8ba0ed7c51e78c6a39b19ad6ddf8d176d2780acd2a2"},"summary":"A store link on Docker with no image fails at its first clone, not at startup","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T19:10:35.497483Z","id":"271d84acde1bfadcde39dc6c236cbacc880d3a285f4267dfab84a1a9841c3ee2","body":{"detail":"A branch is judged finished only when a run starts (ContainerWorkspace::branch_for). A run that began on an open pull request and sees it merged or closed before it proposes pushes to that same branch, finds no open pull request and opens a second one from it, against a base that already holds the first commits. Nothing is lost, and a person reviews the result, but it goes around the rule that a later change starts from the current base on a new branch (docs/usage.md, Connecting a private repository).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1270},"end":{"line":1287},"content_hash":"f5e8fc26a03bc03e83af02a746f456c7fbdc2e7a8b0486bca008aeb28d33190f"},"summary":"A pull request merged during a run leaves that run proposing onto a finished branch","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/preview.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T19:10:35.497516Z","id":"3f7d1b4c26fdeaff811ee730a35bae8869a0e31a689726e82be2474ba56ca7cf","body":{"detail":"preview_url is required of a link (check_preview_url in crates/clax-store/src/queue_repos.rs), so a repository with nothing to deploy has to name an address that never answers. Each fix then stays held for preview_timeout_secs, and only then do the members get PREVIEW_MISSED. Members can hand it over before that. Making preview_url optional would let such a fix say at once that it waits for a person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"3658e876c78259f1ca2fb00b734bdda93f4bd95e6ca273a39a4f4830a6b73cd9"},"summary":"A target with no working preview waits out the whole timeout before anyone is told","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:57:16.727768Z","id":"d125832163b63e49b975d4c2893766d51099bcd0ecaa802287b312924067d650","body":{"detail":"Forge::describe writes the host's block and the model's summary again, so the changed paths match what the branch holds. Anything a person wrote into the body between proposals goes. Replacing only the host's block would need the body read back and a marker the model cannot imitate.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1379},"end":{"line":1379},"content_hash":"3dec6cba01bbf82e7cf1d778d5e91118eed01638b62e059a05744934fdad4d3e"},"summary":"Each proposal replaces the whole pull request text, so a person's edit to it is lost","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T20:57:16.728918Z","id":"c2adb34f7936fc515573963b2131009fb8cec8e74b6d8d53184fdb7f8ec3cbb6","body":{"detail":"HTML comments are stripped and mentions defused, but `Fixes #12` in model text closes that issue on merge, and owner/repo#1 leaves a reference on another repository. The host's block comes first and says what is the model's; the model can still write text imitating it below the line.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":175},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"00adf6f2f92382daa6c8c96658259dedf9c8f3cdfaccfbc995a6ae840a8d7ccd"},"summary":"A summary can still close an issue or cross-reference one","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:34:49.789983Z","id":"6874c0fbaa30ca72e42c2c0e733908846c8b33a3bad1e67320b091ccdf4a3f81","body":{"detail":"ContainerWorkspace::target_private answers apart from the offer, so a source that cannot be read is not taken as private. clax_bot::workspace::Workspace's default reads the offer, and crates/clax-bot-remote has only that: an offer the service made confidential because its source failed reads as private, and PROPOSAL_PUBLIC is skipped. The wire needs the service's own answer, carried beside the offer, before a hosted run on a linked target proposes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1242},"end":{"line":1255},"content_hash":"65f4d91d6f202950dfacc56f9f27b8a8141b2805b85a1a0dd1a5d1fbf6d74a64"},"summary":"A remote workspace answers target_private from its offer, so a target unread by the service reads as private on that path","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:34:49.790135Z","id":"001eff9bfea8231f884e9ad7c8d9c6287c49ba05a8bf7fe9b61ac9a9546d6506","body":{"detail":"proposing is held from before the patch is read until the pull request opens, so one workspace's proposals go one at a time, and a slow container holds the rest for up to PATCH_TIMEOUT. It covers one process: two deployments on one repository can still pass the open pull request cap together, and each keeps its own push count.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1351},"end":{"line":1351},"content_hash":"e1e9324f4f2dd97d7bf4ae5a700acf801dbe8c7451a7f556d431583510d87d23"},"summary":"The lock that keeps two runs off the last pull request is held across take_patch","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:34:49.791395Z","id":"31f1cece2427b3419ce6e40ab4a3e9d5c8b3a04498ba7933e00e42b2ca99bd2a","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Only the host block is rewritten now: a_persons_words_in_a_pull_request_survive_a_later_proposal and a_later_block_replaces_only_the_block pass.","supersedes":"d125832163b63e49b975d4c2893766d51099bcd0ecaa802287b312924067d650","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:34:50.288564Z","id":"c04f7f077fcdeae1c245d610a1df8f605ccb53d65228b6163ebf5b00704b07d8","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Model text is quoted line by line and neutralized: a_closing_keyword_closes_nothing_in_any_form, a_models_line_cannot_pose_as_the_hosts and a_title_closes_nothing_in_the_commit_or_the_pull_request pass.","supersedes":"c2adb34f7936fc515573963b2131009fb8cec8e74b6d8d53184fdb7f8ec3cbb6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T22:10:21.783747Z","id":"7b8416f48f8658eaa7c4cfd74168ccaaa6e06a44c894a5db5a146d4363e5caec","body":{"detail":"Both are written by a workspace.toml's operator, and guidance reaches a system prompt, so a linked target has neither. A queue admin is not an operator: letting one write guidance needs a decision on who may write into a prompt.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":240},"content_hash":"53b64df84ab8d3eebc49163a9aceaa974b4d0a38744d7c9dc0e23bfed69bd8c3"},"summary":"guidance and preview_gate on a repository linked from the queue's panel","tags":["revisit:a linked repository's runs need build guidance that AGENTS.md cannot give","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/forge.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:05:45.311557Z","id":"7394aa14af4ce1a9d59211211c8cd7ff6c002d951765d5c6b301dda23f7fc753","body":{"detail":"commit_subject defuses only #N and GH-N, so that the subject stays a conventional commit and searchable. A subject such as `docs: fixes https://github.com/o/r/issues/1` reaches the commit and the pull request's title unchanged; whether GitHub closes that issue on merge has not been tried. neutralize still covers the pull request's body.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"77ad82d33aa12786d4e6e91bfd81a6f92eff3b7b4d1ca900ee20d54947e9a112"},"summary":"A commit subject keeps a closing word before an issue's address","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/net.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:29:54.570614Z","id":"0e1d5e9541091f1d3506c94246d423f8d982fca350d3fd40960f3b8afe6cd2ce","body":{"detail":"net::tests::a_proxy_in_the_environment_is_not_used passes under bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot-workspace:clax_bot_workspace_lib_test, and failed with 'it went to the proxy' with .no_proxy() removed; git_is_pinned_to_the_public_answers_alone_and_follows_no_redirect asserts the pin. A hosted daemon that leaves its network only through a proxy now reaches no held link. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-06-claxbot-workspace-design.md section 4 still states the old trade.","kind":"resolve","summary":"No proxy on any way out held to PublicOnly: client() sets no_proxy and pin() adds -c http.proxy=","supersedes":"d7bfeff3f44a30e8c601b05e69bcfc633fcf4742682b67a9cf41241b978e558b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/daytona.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T00:30:28.135456Z","id":"d698f147fdb87962fed482c03346e5593d52998eeecb921f5aa8a732fe1b1849","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8ab1456eff59cf9efede309ea4ae22b03d0f6082f608a287635a6a4d483ea2bc","summary":"Added to what only a real run settles, read from Daytona's documentation on 2026-11-06 and not run: that `daytona snapshot push` with --cpu 4 --memory 8 --disk 10 reaches each sandbox made from the snapshot (CreateSnapshot in openapi.json calls them what is 'allocated to the resulting sandbox'); that 10 GB of disk holds the image and a cold build, which peaked at 6.7 GB without saying what the image took; that an amd64 image pushed from an arm64 host runs; and what a snapshot gone inactive after two weeks answers to POST /sandbox. CreateSandbox lists cpu, memory and disk beside snapshot, but the SDKs' from-snapshot parameters have none, so create_body sends none: whether the API takes or refuses them with a snapshot is unknown.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T00:30:28.135778Z","id":"eeacebe33bb3d479c771bc7e90050ca6da860a7e95618daa459c56a57292403c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8641bd89891cd371283a8db647bcd96e79db1885a940879d4efde0912ed6d536","summary":"The same holds on Daytona: check_image now refuses a file target there with no image, and a store link with none still gets Daytona's default snapshot of 1 vCPU, 1 GiB and 3 GiB, since a daemon with no link yet must start.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:30:51.507582Z","id":"0f1260d9d8e4d5f36c153e7b8d7e3b9cb9c184829e3b367d800a5ffd3fb3da21","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8641bd89891cd371283a8db647bcd96e79db1885a940879d4efde0912ed6d536","summary":"Daytona no longer holds as comment eeacebe3 says: check_image now refuses a home on Daytona with no image, or a blank one, target or none, since the linked route's file needs image too (deploy/claxbot-workspace/README.md). A daemon still starts, with no containers and RuntimeFacts.failed set (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs workspace_of). Docker with no target and no image is unchanged, so a store link there still fails at its first clone. Test: config::tests::a_home_on_daytona_needs_a_snapshot_with_no_target.","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T07:10:41.590470Z","id":"ac3612c60cf64c01a5d510b06d3bd66f03d0cefe73b3f964ab2a7e517d78e169","body":{"detail":"by_push passes anything but PushRefused to unavailable(), whose words are 'the container could not be reached; nothing was changed. Try again.' Repo::reach (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/repo.rs) bails on any other git failure, including a connection lost after the remote took the ref. The hold on a run's words is unaffected: proposal_left_nothing (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs) reads no shell_unavailable as proof. What the model reads, and may repeat to the queue's people, can still be false.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":522},"end":{"line":536},"content_hash":"39a09d588db309ff0f9e9a6a9aaa2a5eaf6dff216be1a7e4578c7d8ee36be122"},"suggested_fix":"Give a failed push words of its own that say the push may have landed, as after_push does for what follows it.","summary":"A git push that dies on the network tells the run nothing changed, though the remote may have taken it","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
